1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,279
A shared microphone hears everyone in the room.

2
00:00:02,279 --> 00:00:05,825
But a voice agent should only listen to the people talking to it.

3
00:00:06,667 --> 00:00:09,608
The camera tracks each person and estimates their distance.

4
00:00:09,608 --> 00:00:13,726
Step into the interaction region, and your voice goes through to the agent.

5
00:00:14,583 --> 00:00:17,728
A participant can stop speaking and still be present.

6
00:00:17,728 --> 00:00:20,873
The agent should wait, rather than end the conversation.

7
00:00:21,750 --> 00:00:24,283
Now one person steps out of the region.

8
00:00:24,283 --> 00:00:28,223
The microphone still hears them, but their voice no longer reaches the agent.

9
00:00:29,083 --> 00:00:32,648
Compare the microphone input with the audio passed to the agent.

10
00:00:32,648 --> 00:00:37,698
Voice isolation keeps the near voice, and the camera turns down speech from outside the region.

11
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:41,767
When everyone leaves the region, the conversation can end.

12
00:00:41,767 --> 00:00:48,301
Presence demo uses the camera and voice isolation, so your voice agent hears only the people inside the region.
